hpc:Task a owl:Class .
hpc:Job a owl:Class .
hpc:Node a owl:Class .
hpc:Layout a owl:Class .

# Object properties
hpc:hasTask a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain hpc:Job ;
    rdfs:range hpc:Task .
hpc:isOn a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain hpc:Layout ;
    rdfs:range hpc:Node .

# Datatype properties
hpc:taskID a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain hpc:Task ;
    rdfs:range xsd:integer .
hpc:nodeID a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain hpc:Node ;
    rdfs:range xsd:integer .
hpc:layout a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain hpc:Layout ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

# Subclass relations
hpc:ArbitraryJob a hpc:Job ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Class ;
                      owl:intersectionOf (hpc:Job hpc:ArbitraryLayout) ] .

hpc:ArbitraryLayout a hpc:Layout ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Class ;
                      owl:intersectionOf (hpc:Layout hpc:ArbitraryTaskCount) ] .

hpc:ArbitraryTaskCount a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Class ;
                      owl:onProperty hpc:hasTask ;
                      owl:someValuesFrom (hpc:ArbitraryTaskDistribution) ] .

hpc:ArbitraryTaskDistribution a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Class ;
                      owl:onProperty hpc:isOn ;
                      owl:cardinality (1|*) ] .
```

This ontology fragment defines classes for HPC tasks, jobs, nodes, and layouts. It also defines object properties for the relationships between jobs, tasks, nodes, and layouts, as well as datatype properties for task ID, node ID, and layout. The ontology also includes subclass relations for jobs and layouts that have specific characteristics, such as arbitrary task distribution and count.
